IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `crm-time`

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth) -- sections 4C, 4G, 4H, 4J and 4JA:
-- offences under two or more laws, indictable and summary offences, and the
-- dealing with certain indictable offences in a court of summary jurisdiction.
--
-- Each rule answers MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER. JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE
-- only where the text says so in its own words ("unless", "if", "does not
-- apply", "shall not", "cannot"); NOTHING where the text lists without closing
-- the list, limits its reach without "only", or does not speak. A rule that
-- yields a number sits beside the rule that decides whether the provision
-- applies at all.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) ss 4C-4JA: offences under several laws, and summary dealing`

§§ `Section 4C: offences under 2 or more laws`

DECLARE OverlapOfLaws IS ONE OF
    `2 or more laws of the Commonwealth`
    `a law of the Commonwealth and the common law`
    `some other combination of laws`

-- src:4383 | (1) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence:
-- src:4384 | (a) under 2 or more laws of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:4385 | (b) both under a law of the Commonwealth and at common law;
-- src:4386 | the offender shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws of the Commonwealth or at common law, but shall not be liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission.
@ref s 4C(1) (src:4383-4386)
GIVEN `the overlap` IS AN OverlapOfLaws
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws` IS
    CONSIDER `the overlap`
    WHEN `some other combination of laws` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4383 | (1) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence:
-- src:4384 | (a) under 2 or more laws of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:4385 | (b) both under a law of the Commonwealth and at common law;
-- src:4386 | the offender shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be liable to be prosecuted and punished under either or any of those laws of the Commonwealth or at common law, but shall not be liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission.
@ref s 4C(1) (src:4383-4386)
GIVEN `the overlap` IS AN OverlapOfLaws
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4C(1) the offender is liable to be punished twice for the same act or omission` IS
    CONSIDER `the overlap`
    WHEN `some other combination of laws` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4387 | (2) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under both:
-- src:4388 | (a) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a State; or
-- src:4389 | (b) a law of the Commonwealth and a law of a Territory;
-- src:4390 | and the offender has been punished for that offence under the law of the State or the law of the Territory, as the case may be, the offender shall not be liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 4C(2) (src:4387-4390)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence under a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is an offence under a law of a State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is an offence under a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has been punished for that offence under the law of the State or the law of the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4C(2) the offender is liable to be punished for the offence under the law of the Commonwealth` IS
    IF `the act or omission is an offence under a law of the Commonwealth`
       AND (`the act or omission is an offence under a law of a State` OR `the act or omission is an offence under a law of a Territory`)
       AND `the offender has been punished for that offence under the law of the State or the law of the Territory`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4391 | (3) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence against a law of a Territory, the validity of that law is not affected merely because the act or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 4C(3) (src:4391)
GIVEN `the act or omission is an offence against a law of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only ground of challenge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4C(3) the validity of that law is affected` IS
    IF `the act or omission is an offence against a law of a Territory` AND `the act or omission also constitutes an offence against a law of the Commonwealth` AND `that is the only ground of challenge`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Sections 4G and 4H: indictable offences and summary offences`

-- The band of the maximum term of imprisonment is worked out in crm-time.l4.
-- A term for life, and a term the text does not state as a period, have no band.

-- src:4409 | Offences against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 12 months are indictable offences, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 4G (src:4409)
GIVEN `the offence is against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4G the offence is an indictable offence` IS
    IF NOT `the offence is against a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the band of a term of imprisonment` `the term`
              WHEN JUST `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST `more than 10 years` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4411 | Offences against a law of the Commonwealth, being offences which:
-- src:4412 | (a) are punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months; or
-- src:4413 | (b) are not punishable by imprisonment;
-- src:4414 | are summary offences, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 4H (src:4411-4414)
GIVEN `the offence is against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4H the offence is a summary offence` IS
    IF NOT `the offence is against a law of the Commonwealth`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the band of a term of imprisonment` `the term`
              WHEN JUST `not punishable by imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST `12 months or less` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4J: certain indictable offences may be dealt with summarily`

DECLARE CriminalCodeOffence IS ONE OF
    `an offence against Division 80 of the Criminal Code (other than Subdivision CA)`
    `an offence against Subdivision CA of Division 80 of the Criminal Code`
    `an offence against Division 82 of the Criminal Code`
    `an offence against Division 91 of the Criminal Code`
    `an offence against Division 92 of the Criminal Code`
    `an offence against another provision`

-- src:4427 | (7) This section does not apply to an offence against:
-- src:4428 | (b) Division 80 (other than Subdivision CA) of the Criminal Code (treason, urging violence and advocating terrorism or genocide); or
-- src:4429 | (c) Division 82 of the Criminal Code (sabotage); or
-- src:4430 | (d) Division 91 of the Criminal Code (espionage); or
-- src:4431 | (e) Division 92 of the Criminal Code (foreign interference).
@ref s 4J(7) (src:4427-4431)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A CriminalCodeOffence
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(7) section 4J does not apply to the offence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence against Division 80 of the Criminal Code (other than Subdivision CA)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an offence against Division 82 of the Criminal Code` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an offence against Division 91 of the Criminal Code` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an offence against Division 92 of the Criminal Code` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "an offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000": the
-- value is NOTHING where the offence does not relate to property.
-- src:4421 | (4) A court of summary jurisdiction may, if it thinks fit, upon the request of the prosecutor, hear and determine any proceeding in respect of an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000.
@ref s 4J(4) (src:4421)
GIVEN `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(4) the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000` IF
    CONSIDER `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST v THEN v AT MOST `the value of property, in dollars, that an indictable offence may not exceed for s 4J(4)`

-- src:4416 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an offence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the Commonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention appears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.
@ref s 4J(1) (src:4416)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(1) the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant is given` IS
    IF `the prosecutor consents` AND `the defendant consents` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4416 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an offence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the Commonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention appears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.
-- src:4417 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to an indictable offence where, under a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act, that offence may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction.
@ref s 4J(1) (src:4416-4417)
GIVEN `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
      `the offence is one to which subsection (4) refers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act lets a court of summary jurisdiction hear and determine the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one to which s 4J(7) says section 4J does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(1) a court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine the indictable offence` IS
    IF `the offence is one to which s 4J(7) says section 4J does not apply`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth` AND `the offence is one to which subsection (4) refers`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth` AND `a law of the Commonwealth other than this Act lets a court of summary jurisdiction hear and determine the offence`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF NOT `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth`
                   THEN NOTHING
                   ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
                        THEN JUST FALSE
                        ELSE CONSIDER `the band of a term of imprisonment` `the term`
                             WHEN JUST `12 months or less` THEN `s 4J(1) the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant is given` `the prosecutor consents` `the defendant consents`
                             WHEN JUST `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years` THEN `s 4J(1) the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant is given` `the prosecutor consents` `the defendant consents`
                             WHEN JUST `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years` THEN `s 4J(1) the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant is given` `the prosecutor consents` `the defendant consents`
                             OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4418 | (3) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1), the court may impose:
-- src:4419 | (a) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both; or
-- src:4420 | (b) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 5 years but not exceeding 10 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(3) (src:4418-4420)
GIVEN `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(3) the most months of imprisonment the court may impose` IS
    IF NOT `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the band of a term of imprisonment` `the term`
         WHEN JUST `12 months or less` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(a) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         WHEN JUST `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(a) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         WHEN JUST `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(b) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4418 | (3) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1), the court may impose:
-- src:4419 | (a) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both; or
-- src:4420 | (b) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 5 years but not exceeding 10 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(3) (src:4418-4420)
GIVEN `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(3) the most penalty units of fine the court may impose` IS
    IF NOT `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the band of a term of imprisonment` `the term`
         WHEN JUST `12 months or less` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(a) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         WHEN JUST `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(a) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         WHEN JUST `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years` THEN JUST `s 4J(3)(b) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4421 | (4) A court of summary jurisdiction may, if it thinks fit, upon the request of the prosecutor, hear and determine any proceeding in respect of an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000.
@ref s 4J(4) (src:4421)
GIVEN `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the prosecutor requests it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one to which s 4J(7) says section 4J does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(4) a court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine the proceeding` IS
    IF `the offence is one to which s 4J(7) says section 4J does not apply`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `the offence is an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `s 4J(4) the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000` `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars` AND `the prosecutor requests it` AND `the court thinks fit`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4422 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4), the court may impose a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(5) (src:4422)
GIVEN `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(5) the most months of imprisonment the court may impose` IS
    IF `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST `s 4J(5) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4422 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4), the court may impose a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(5) (src:4422)
GIVEN `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(5) the most penalty units of fine the court may impose` IS
    IF `the offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST `s 4J(5) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (6)(a) and (b): the limit under (3) or (5) is not to exceed what
-- could have been imposed on trial on indictment.
-- src:4423 | (6) A court of summary jurisdiction shall not impose under subsection (3) or (5):
-- src:4424 | (a) a sentence of imprisonment for a period exceeding the maximum period that could have been imposed had the offence been tried on indictment;
@ref s 4J(6)(a) (src:4423-4424)
GIVEN `the most months under subsection (3) or (5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum term that could have been imposed had the offence been tried on indictment` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(6)(a) the most months of imprisonment the court may impose` IS
    CONSIDER `the term of imprisonment expressed in months` `the maximum term that could have been imposed had the offence been tried on indictment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST m THEN JUST (IF m LESS THAN `the most months under subsection (3) or (5)` THEN m ELSE `the most months under subsection (3) or (5)`)

-- src:4423 | (6) A court of summary jurisdiction shall not impose under subsection (3) or (5):
-- src:4424 | (a) a sentence of imprisonment for a period exceeding the maximum period that could have been imposed had the offence been tried on indictment;
-- src:4425 | (b) a fine exceeding the maximum fine that could have been imposed had the offence been so tried; or
@ref s 4J(6)(b) (src:4423-4425)
GIVEN `the most penalty units under subsection (3) or (5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum fine that could have been imposed had the offence been so tried, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4J(6)(b) the most penalty units of fine the court may impose` IS
    IF `the maximum fine that could have been imposed had the offence been so tried, in penalty units` LESS THAN `the most penalty units under subsection (3) or (5)`
    THEN `the maximum fine that could have been imposed had the offence been so tried, in penalty units`
    ELSE `the most penalty units under subsection (3) or (5)`

-- src:4423 | (6) A court of summary jurisdiction shall not impose under subsection (3) or (5):
-- src:4424 | (a) a sentence of imprisonment for a period exceeding the maximum period that could have been imposed had the offence been tried on indictment;
-- src:4425 | (b) a fine exceeding the maximum fine that could have been imposed had the offence been so tried; or
-- src:4426 | (c) both a sentence of imprisonment and a fine if the offence is punishable on trial on indictment by a sentence of imprisonment or a fine, but not both.
@ref s 4J(6)(c) (src:4423-4426)
GIVEN `the offence is punishable on trial on indictment by a sentence of imprisonment or a fine, but not both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4J(6)(c) the court may impose both a sentence of imprisonment and a fine` IS
    IF `the offence is punishable on trial on indictment by a sentence of imprisonment or a fine, but not both`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 4JA: some indictable offences punishable by fine only`

DECLARE DefendantKind IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

-- 4JA(1)(b): "not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000
-- penalty units for a body corporate".
-- src:4435 | (b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate; and
@ref s 4JA(1)(b) (src:4435)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty for the offence, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4JA(1)(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than the limit` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `the pecuniary penalty for the offence, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(1)(b) the most penalty units for an individual`
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN `the pecuniary penalty for the offence, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(1)(b) the most penalty units for a body corporate`

-- src:4441 | (3) This section has effect subject to any contrary intention indicated by the law creating the offence.
@ref s 4JA(3) (src:4441)
GIVEN `the law creating the offence indicates a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4JA(3) this section has effect` IS
    IF `the law creating the offence indicates a contrary intention` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4442 | (4) Without limiting subsection (3), this section does not apply to an indictable offence:
-- src:4443 | (a) created by a law that provides that the offence may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction; or
@ref s 4JA(4)(a) (src:4442-4443)
GIVEN `the offence is created by a law that provides that it may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4JA(4)(a) this section does not apply to the offence` IS
    IF `the offence is created by a law that provides that it may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4444 | (b) described in subsection 4J(4) (about offences relating to property valued at $5,000 or less).
@ref s 4JA(4)(b) (src:4444)
GIVEN `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4JA(4)(b) the offence is described in subsection 4J(4)` IF
    `s 4J(4) the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000` `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars`

-- src:4433 | (1) A court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine an indictable offence if:
-- src:4434 | (a) the offence is not punishable by imprisonment; and
-- src:4435 | (b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate; and
-- src:4436 | (c) the defendant and prosecution consent.
@ref s 4JA(1) (src:4433-4436)
GIVEN `the offence is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is punishable by imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty for the offence, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
      `the defendant and prosecution consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law creating the offence indicates a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is created by a law that provides that it may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4JA(1) a court of summary jurisdiction may hear and determine the indictable offence` IS
    IF NOT `the offence is an indictable offence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (`s 4JA(3) this section has effect` `the law creating the offence indicates a contrary intention` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              OR (`s 4JA(4)(a) this section does not apply to the offence` `the offence is created by a law that provides that it may be heard and determined by a court of summary jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
              OR `s 4JA(4)(b) the offence is described in subsection 4J(4)` `the value of the property to which the offence relates, in dollars`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (NOT `the offence is punishable by imprisonment`)
                 AND `s 4JA(1)(b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than the limit` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty for the offence, in penalty units`
                 AND `the defendant and prosecution consent`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Subsection (2). Both paragraphs say "not more than N penalty units ... if the
-- offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more
-- than M": an offence whose penalty on indictment is not more than 300 penalty
-- units for an individual (1,500 for a body corporate) also satisfies the
-- condition of paragraph (b), which is satisfied by up to 600 (3,000). Read
-- literally, with "or" between the paragraphs, the court may impose the
-- greatest amount for which the condition of any paragraph is met. The same
-- rule is given below on the narrower reading in which paragraph (a) applies
-- to the lower band and paragraph (b) only above it. The closing sentence
-- ("However ...") caps the amount at the penalty on indictment.
-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
@ref s 4JA(2)(a) (src:4438)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose` IS
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
        IF `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units on indictment for an individual`
        THEN JUST `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose on an individual`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
        IF `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units on indictment for a body corporate`
        THEN JUST `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose on a body corporate`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2)(b) (src:4439)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose` IS
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
        IF `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units on indictment for an individual`
        THEN JUST `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose on an individual`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
        IF `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` AT MOST `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units on indictment for a body corporate`
        THEN JUST `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose on a body corporate`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- The closing sentence of subsection (2): "the court may not impose a
-- pecuniary penalty greater than the penalty that could have been imposed if
-- the offence had been prosecuted on indictment".
-- src:4440 | However, the court may not impose a pecuniary penalty greater than the penalty that could have been imposed if the offence had been prosecuted on indictment.
@ref s 4JA(2) (src:4440)
GIVEN `the limit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4JA(2) the limit after the closing sentence` IS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (IF `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` LESS THAN n THEN `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` ELSE n)

-- src:4437 | (2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary penalty of:
-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2) (src:4437-4439)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4JA(2) the most penalty units the court may impose, on the reading that either paragraph may be used` IS
    `s 4JA(2) the limit after the closing sentence` (`the greater of the two limits`) `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
    WHERE
        `the greater of the two limits` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
            WHEN JUST a THEN CONSIDER `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
                             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
                             WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (IF a LESS THAN b THEN b ELSE a)

-- src:4437 | (2) If the defendant is convicted, the court may impose a pecuniary penalty of:
-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2) (src:4437-4439)
GIVEN `the defendant` IS A DefendantKind
      `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 4JA(2) the most penalty units the court may impose, on the reading that paragraph (a) governs the lower band` IS
    `s 4JA(2) the limit after the closing sentence` (`the band limit`) `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
    WHERE
        `the band limit` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
            WHEN JUST a THEN JUST a
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose` `the defendant` `the pecuniary penalty on indictment, in penalty units`
